# ADR-0257: three changes to one file, arriving together.
#
# A keystroke is a `didChange` carrying the whole document, so a client typing
# faster than the compiler runs leaves several of them queued. Compiling all
# but the last is work whose answer is stale before it could be published --
# 933 ms of it, measured against a 22 900-line source, and the reason this row
# of `doc/roadmap.md` named a concurrency construct.
#
# What is pinned here is that **one** `publishDiagnostics` comes back and it
# is the last change's. Three would mean nothing is coalesced; none would mean
# the drain swallowed the work. It needs no clock and no timing, which is what
# makes it a golden at all: the whole session is available at once, so what
# has "already arrived" is deterministic.
#
# It is also why the server only ever *drains what is there*. Waiting for more
# would be a policy about a client's typing speed; reading what has already
# arrived is a fact about the queue.

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"processId":null,"rootUri":null,"capabilities":{}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"initialized","params":{}}

# The document as opened, which is analysed on its own.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didOpen","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas","languageId":"pascal","version":1,"text":"program p(output);\nbegin writeln('a') end.\n"}}}

# Three changes, back to back. Only the third is compiled.
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didChange","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas","version":2},"contentChanges":[{"text":"program p(output);\nbegin writeln(nope1) end.\n"}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didChange","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas","version":3},"contentChanges":[{"text":"program p(output);\nbegin writeln(nope2) end.\n"}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"textDocument/didChange","params":{"textDocument":{"uri":"file:///scratch/hello.pas","version":4},"contentChanges":[{"text":"program p(output);\nbegin writeln(final) end.\n"}]}}

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"shutdown"}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"exit"}
